Package: RegCompassR
Title: Multiome Regulatory Evidence and Metabolic Reaction Analysis
Version: 2.3.0
Authors@R: c(person(given = "RegCompass", family = "Developers", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "dev@example.com"))
Author: RegCompass Developers [aut, cre]
Maintainer: RegCompass Developers <dev@example.com>
Description: Integrates paired single-cell RNA and ATAC regulatory evidence
    with genome-scale metabolic reaction analysis. Stage 1 fixes min_cells at
    300 and applies the same cell set before normalization and downstream
    metacell construction. With two or more conditions, each broad cell type
    uses one canonical Pando condition-GRN procedure: candidate edges are
    discovered on the complete cell type and separately in every condition,
    exact TF-peak-target triples are unioned into one frozen dictionary, and
    every condition is refitted with the same unscaled Gaussian identity Pando
    interaction model. Condition effects retain their fitted coefficient,
    standard error, P value and BH-adjusted P value. Only coefficients with
    adjusted P below 0.05 and acceptable target model fit enter the regulatory
    penalty. No pooled-coefficient rescaling, nested condition cross-validation,
    sparse-group path, structural-zero coefficient substitution or common-
    support decomposition is used. When no condition is supplied or fewer than
    two levels are observed, Stage 1 directly fits the original Pando GRN within
    each broad cell type and creates no condition coefficient. Paired-cell
    TF-by-ATAC regulatory effects are projected before exact SuperCell
    aggregation. Metacells use one multimodal WNN graph per broad cell type and
    remain condition-pure after membership splitting. RNA support, regulatory
    effects, GPR rules, shared union GEM construction and directional metabolic
    penalties use consistent reaction ordering, bounds and medium scenarios.
